. Xavier Becerra leads Steve Hilton by 18 to 25 points in every poll conducted since mid-August, including large surveys from Berkeley IGS, PPIC, and SurveyUSA. All seven expert raters place the contest in the Solid or Safe Democratic column, and prediction markets on both Kalshi and PredictIt price Becerra's chances at about 96 percent.\n\nHilton, a political newcomer and former broadcaster, has matched Becerra in fundraising and centers his campaign on affordability and cost of living, the top voter concern in recent polling. But headlines consistently describe him as a clear underdog, and his best opening is lagging Democratic enthusiasm rather than any movement in the polls. The state's twelve-point Democratic lean points to a comfortable Becerra victory, with the main question being the size of the margin.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9963, "margin": 17.38}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.998, "margin": 20.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9982, "margin": 20.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.998, "margin": 21.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9936, "margin": 19.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9916, "margin": 19.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.996, "margin": 19.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.9966, "margin": 19.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9966, "margin": 20.0}]}